  "label": "The man is mapped as someone who can skip prison by playing his cards right",
  "description": "The overlaid text 'if you play your cards right you can skip prison' is directly mapped onto the visual entity 'man'. The text implies that the man is the one who used manipulation or deceit to avoid legal consequences, thereby projecting the textual concept of 'someone who can skip prison by playing their cards right' onto the visual representation of the man. This is an analogical mapping where the man is the entity being described by the text.",
